abstract: >-
  Analysis code, generated results and figures for four experiments on the
  validity boundaries of grouped discrete-time hazard models for degradation
  data. (1) Effective calibration information for every cross-domain transport
  split, showing that labelled target count does not determine the information
  available to estimate a calibration slope. (2) A 225-cell recalibration
  boundary study varying event prevalence and prediction spread independently
  of labelled sample size. (3) A complementary log-log, logit and probit link
  comparison on a 493-cell lithium-ion corpus. (4) Wiener and gamma
  first-passage degradation baselines compared like-for-like against the
  discrete-time hazard model.
